= Economic Message and Program

Voters do not just want a defense of norms; they want an economy that works for them. What do we propose?

- @middle_class: Middle-class tax relief and childcare
- @industrial_policy: Industrial policy and reshoring
- @green_new_deal: A climate jobs program
- @fiscal_hawk: Credibility on deficits
- @easy_discard

@middle_class
on-arrival: economic_plan = 1; working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); suburban_dem += 4*(1-dissent); moderate_strength += 2; crisis_urgency += 1; month_actions += 1

We lay out tax credits and childcare support for working families.

@industrial_policy
on-arrival: economic_plan = 1; working_dem += 4*(1-dissent); rural_dem += 2*(1-dissent); labor_strength += 2; populist_strength += 2; abundance_dissent += 2; crisis_urgency += 1; month_actions += 1

We invest in factories, supply chains, and apprenticeships.

@green_new_deal
on-arrival: economic_plan = 1; young_dem += 4*(1-dissent); educated_dem += 3*(1-dissent); progressive_strength += 3; rural_dem -= 1*(1-dissent); biz_relation -= 2; climate_agenda += 1; crisis_urgency += 1; month_actions += 1

A big program of green investment energizes the young but frightens energy workers.

@fiscal_hawk
on-arrival: economic_plan = 1; suburban_dem += 3*(1-dissent); biz_relation += 5; progressive_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 3; budget += 1; month_actions += 1

We pair promises with offsets. Voters reward seriousness; activists call it timidity.
